{"diagnosis": "Loopback RX got 0xff (idle) instead of 0xa5, so ser_tx never presented correct start/data bits. TX bit-advance on line 130 uses (cfg_divider >> 4) - the 16x RX oversample tick - instead of full cfg_divider. With divider 64 TX shifts every ~5 cycles vs 64 expected, so the peer samples idle and the transfer fails.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
 				send_bitcnt <= 10;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
-			if (send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) && send_bitcnt) begin
+			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5 with no uart data mismatch TRAP"}

